throughout their course. The corrected platelet count increments (CCI) were calculated for the first 25 transfusions of 
each patient and non-immune factors present at the time of each platelet transfusion were documented. The mean CCI for  
the first 25 transfusions in the ABO-identical group was significantly higher (6600 +/- 7900 SD) than that achieved with
ABO unmatched platelets (5200 +/- 7900; p < 0.01). The effect was most marked for the first 10 transfusions for each    
patient where the CCI was 64% higher in the ABO-identical group (8200 +/- 7500 vs 5000 +/- 8100; p < 0.0002). Patients  
given ABO-identical platelets required only about half as many transfusions in the first 30 days (10 versus 17, p <     
0.05) or during the first admission (11 versus 21 p < 0.01) as patients in the ABO-unmatched group. A smaller percentage
